@startuml
title 06 — Guardrails & Error Handling

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' This diagram is referenced by Diagram 02 and Diagram 04.
'
' The Orchestrator applies three layers of protection on every
' planning request, in this order:
'
'   Layer 1 — Permission check
'     Is this user allowed to use the system at all?
'
'   Layer 2 — Input guard
'     Is the message safe and within policy?
'     Checks for prompt-injection attempts, blocked content patterns,
'     and PII (email, phone, SSN, card numbers — masked, not rejected).
'
'   Layer 3 — Output guard
'     Before the Business Agent's response is shown to the user,
'     does it contain anything it shouldn't (secrets, credentials, PII)?
'
' Any layer that fails sends an error to the user and stops processing.
'
' Error code reference
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' ORCH_001  Could not understand the request — message was too unclear
' ORCH_004  Business Agent response failed the output quality check
' ORCH_005  User does not have permission to perform this action
' ORCH_006  Message was flagged by the input safety check
' ORCH_011  Request is not something the system can handle; try rephrasing
' ORCH_003  Business Agent took too long to respond (timeout)
' ORCH_009  Unexpected error occurred during processing
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

hide footbox
autonumber "<b>[00]"

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam wrapWidth 260
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor        #2D6A9F
  ArrowFontColor    #2D6A9F
  ArrowFontSize     11

  LifeLineBorderColor         #2D6A9F
  LifeLineBackgroundColor     #EAF3FB

  ParticipantBorderColor      #2D6A9F
  ParticipantBackgroundColor  #DAEAF7
  ParticipantFontColor        #1A3A52
  ParticipantFontSize         12
  ParticipantFontStyle        bold
  ParticipantPadding          8
  ParticipantBorderThickness  1.5

  GroupBorderColor            #5A9ABF
  GroupBackgroundColor        #F0F7FC
  GroupHeaderFontColor        #1A3A52
  GroupHeaderFontSize         12
  GroupBorderThickness        1.2

  NoteBackgroundColor         #FFF8DC
  NoteBorderColor             #C8A800
  NoteFontColor               #4A3800
  NoteFontSize                11
}

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

' ─── Participants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
participant Orch as "Orchestrator"
participant Push as "Push Gateway"
database    DB   as "HANA DB"

' ─── Entry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
note over Orch
  Entry point: the background worker has picked up a "begin planning"
  job and is about to start. These three checks always run first,
  before any AI planning or Agent Registry calls happen.
end note

' ─── Layer 1 — Permission ────────────────────────────────────────────
Orch -> Orch : [Layer 1 — Permission]\nIs this user allowed to use the system?

alt #FDF3F3 Permission denied → ORCH_005
  note right of Orch : User does not have permission\nfor this action.
  Orch -> Push : send "You don't have permission\nto perform this action"\n(ORCH_005)

else #EAF6EA Permission granted — move to Layer 2

  ' ─── Layer 2 — Input Guard ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Orch -> Orch : [Layer 2 — Input Guard]\nIs the message safe and within policy?\n\nChecks run in this order:\n  • Empty or over-length message\n  • Prompt injection attempt\n    (e.g. "ignore previous instructions")\n  • Blocked content pattern\n    (e.g. requests to generate malware)\n  • PII detection — emails, phones, card numbers\n    (masked and allowed through, not rejected)

  alt #FDF3F3 Message blocked → ORCH_006
    note right of Orch : Message matched a blocked pattern\nor a prompt injection attempt.
    Orch -> Push : send "Your message was flagged\nby our safety system"\n(ORCH_006)

  else #EAF6EA Message accepted (PII masked if found) — move to core processing

    ' ─── Core Processing ───────────────────────────────────────────
    Orch -> Orch : run planning, task dispatch, and workflow\n

    ' ─── Layer 3 — Output Guard ────────────────────────────────────
    Orch -> Orch : [Layer 3 — Output Guard]\nDoes the Business Agent's response\ncontain anything it should not?\n\nChecks run in this order:\n  • Required fields present (message + status)\n  • PII in output (masked before delivery)\n  • Secrets or credentials in output\n    (API keys, private keys, tokens)

    alt #FDF3F3 Response blocked → ORCH_004
      note right of Orch : Response contained policy-violating\ncontent or failed schema validation.
      Orch -> Push : send "The response didn't pass quality\nchecks — please try again"\n(ORCH_004)

    else #EAF6EA Response accepted — deliver to user
      Orch -> DB   : save conversation state changes
      Orch -> Push : send the (sanitised) response to user
    end

  end
end

@enduml
